---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { KOFI_URL, REPO_URL } from '../../config.js';
import { provider } from '../../legal.js';
const p = provider();
---
<Legal locale="en" route="privacy" title="Privacy policy" description="What is processed when you visit the Nemo website: no cookies, no tracking, hosting by Cloudflare.">
  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>
    {p.name} (address see <a href="/en/imprint">imprint</a>)<br />
    E-mail: <a href="mailto:sven.nemo0@gmail.com">sven.nemo0@gmail.com</a>
  </p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This website sets no cookies, uses no analytics and loads no scripts, fonts or content from third-party servers.</li>
    <li>Your light/dark theme choice is stored only in your browser (localStorage) and never transmitted.</li>
    <li>When the page is requested, the hosting provider processes technically necessary connection data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hosting (Cloudflare Pages)</h2>
  <p>
    The website is served by Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA (in the EU: Cloudflare Germany GmbH, Rosental 7, 80331 Munich).
    When you visit, Cloudflare processes connection data such as IP address, time, requested address, browser identifier and transferred data volume to deliver the page
    and protect it against attacks. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in secure, fast operation). Cloudflare is certified under the EU-US Data
    Privacy Framework; standard contractual clauses apply in addition. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Downloads and links to GitHub</h2>
  <p>
    The download buttons lead directly to GitHub (GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA), where the app files are hosted, and to the
    source code at <a href={REPO_URL} rel="noopener">{REPO_URL}</a>. GitHub processes your data only once you click;
    see <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Support via Ko-fi</h2>
  <p>
    The “Support on Ko-fi” link leads to <a href={KOFI_URL} rel="noopener">Ko-fi</a> (Ko-fi Labs Ltd, United Kingdom), an external provider. This website itself
    processes no payment or contact data. What Ko-fi processes is described in <a href="https://more.ko-fi.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Ko-fi’s privacy policy</a>.
    After a contribution you receive the supporter code at the e-mail address given to Ko-fi; a small service run by the operator (a Cloudflare Worker) processes Ko-fi's notification, sends the e-mail through the mail service Resend (Resend, Inc., USA) and stores no payment data, names or addresses in clear text (hashed check values only, for 400 days). Resend processes your e-mail address and the code for delivery.
  </p>

  <h2>The Nemo app</h2>
  <p>
    The app stores its data on your device. It has no account and no service run by the operator that receives app data. Anything it sends beyond that happens only
    when you set it up or click it (exceptions: update check and currency tool, see below). The full list is in the app under “Settings → About Nemo → Legal → Privacy
    notices” (shown in the app language). Otherwise this policy covers the website only; the recipients below process data under their own privacy rules.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sync (optional):</strong> only to a server you run yourself; end-to-end encrypted with a passphrase.</li>
    <li><strong>Update check:</strong> the Windows and Android apps ask GitHub for the version file (at most once a day, can be switched off); no app data, GitHub sees your IP address.</li>
    <li><strong>AI provider (optional):</strong> only with a provider you set up (e.g. Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini, Groq, OpenRouter, Mistral): your question, the date and the field names of the modules, never your entries. In chat, the chat text goes to the provider. With a local model or Ollama nothing leaves the device. Everything can be switched off with “KI abschalten”.</li>
    <li><strong>Google connection (optional, Windows):</strong> sign-in with your own Google application, read only (calendar: <code>calendar.readonly</code>, email headers: <code>gmail.readonly</code>); the data goes from Google straight to your device. If your Google project is in “Testing” status, the sign-in expires after 7 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Calendar subscription (optional):</strong> fetching the iCal address you enter.</li>
    <li><strong>Model download (optional):</strong> the built-in language model is downloaded from Hugging Face after you confirm.</li>
    <li><strong>Currency tool:</strong> when opened, euro rates are requested from frankfurter.dev, without any app data.</li>
    <li><strong>Supporter code:</strong> only checked on the device; the service that emails it is described above under Ko-fi.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and objection (Art. 15–21 GDPR), and the right to lodge a complaint
    with a supervisory authority. The competent one is the Bavarian State Office for Data Protection Supervision (BayLDA), Promenade 18, 91522 Ansbach, Germany,
    <a href="https://www.lda.bayern.de/" rel="noopener">www.lda.bayern.de</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What usually belongs here in Germany</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    For orientation, not legal advice: name and contact of the controller, processing by the hosting provider (server logs, legal basis, third-country transfer),
    every external service (here only via links: GitHub, Ko-fi), whether cookies or tracking are used, data subject rights and the supervisory authority. Last updated: 6 October 2026.
  </p>
</Legal>
